seg-619366049a16 = Each capability from the table above, in a few lines: what it does, one command to run it, one picture drawn from a real run of the engine, and what the ledger holds for it. The pictures are written by <a1><c1/></a1> into <a2><c2/></a2> (never drawn by hand): <c3/> rewrites them from a built engine, and <c4/> fails if one is stale or its caption here differs. Where an input is a log, it is a made-up one the script writes, because the real third-party logs are never vendored, and the caption says so. Everything below is advisory: not certified, not a type approval, and nothing transmits. A status names what was checked and nothing more; <a3>how a label is earned</a3>.

