seg-2ca727430208 = A <c1/> scenario is a <b>measurement-domain</b> simulation: for each visible satellite it synthesises the pseudorange <c2/> and the L1 Doppler, with the <b>Klobuchar</b> single-frequency ionosphere (<c3/>, IS-GPS-200 §{ "20.3.3.5.2.5" }) and the <b>Saastamoinen</b> zenith troposphere projected by the <b>Niell ({ "1996" })</b> mapping function (<c4/>). The residuals feed <b>snapshot RAIM</b> for per-epoch HPL/VPL, and every satellite's pseudorange, Doppler, C/N₀, and iono/tropo corrections are emitted in the JSON <c5/> array. It is a forward simulator (it generates measurements from a known truth), not a receiver/solver — a zero-noise run reproduces geometry plus the corrections to sub-millimetre (see <c6/>).

