seg-49cadf7f7bf2 = A <c1/> scenario models RF interference as a <b>link budget</b>: a <c2/> (ECEF position, transmit <c3/>, type) raises the jammer-to-signal ratio at a <c4/> watching a Walker <c5/>. From the geometry (free-space path loss and the per-direction receive-antenna gain) it computes each satellite's <c6/>, the <b>effective C/N₀</b> via the standard anti-jam equation (despreading processing gain × the spectral-separation factor <c7/>; Kaplan & Hegarty §{ "9.4" }), and flags loss of lock below a configurable tracking threshold — reporting an <c8/> figure of merit. A { "10" } W broadband jammer at { "1" } km denies the receiver entirely (J/S ≈ { "72" } dB); the same jammer at { "100" } km only degrades the links (see <c9/>).

