seg-a9f0811371b2 = <b>Every chart is self-describing.</b> The browser playground, the CLI's <c1/> export, and the HTML (HyperText Markup Language) scorecard all stamp each chart image with a footer reading <c2/>. The <c3/> is the first { "12" } hex characters of the run's <b>scenario hash</b> — a SHA-256 (the 256-bit Secure Hash Algorithm) digest over the canonical scenario definition (seed, thresholds, model parameters, GNSS windows, …); the integrity and lunar reports, which carry no hash of their own, fall back to a SHA-256 of the scenario source. It is the <b>same fingerprint</b> shown in the one-line summary and the result JSON, so a saved or pasted chart always carries its version, the exact scenario that produced it (for bit-for-bit reproduction), and the source — change any input and the hash changes.

